# Dustfile — Enaction Engine cleanup and hygiene contractile

@abstract:
Cleanup rules that keep the early engine honest, coherent, and free of
speculative or generated residue.
@end

## Hygiene

### no-identity-drift
- description: Canonical project, repository, package, crate, and URL identities agree
- verification: run the identity searches documented in README.adoc
- severity: blocking

### no-speculative-crates
- description: Every workspace crate has implemented behaviour and tests
- verification: inspect Cargo workspace membership and each crate's tests
- severity: blocking

### no-generated-build-artifacts
- description: Cargo target output and generated temporary files are not committed
- verification: git status --short
- severity: warning

### no-stale-provider-badges
- description: External badges are published only after their canonical provider targets exist
- verification: verify each badge target before adding it to README.adoc
- severity: warning

### documentation-templates-aligned
- description: Documentation templates carry the canonical project identity and links
- verification: review docs-template against README.adoc and repository metadata
- severity: warning

### no-duplicate-readme-format
- description: Contractile documentation uses the canonical AsciiDoc format
- verification: test ! -f .machine_readable/contractiles/README.md
- severity: info
